{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And behold, the staff of Aharon had blossomed.</b> It implies that there were two aspects of blossoming there: on one side it blossomed and those blossoms remained permanently and never fell, and on the other side 'ויצא פרח' and fell as is the way of all tree blossoms — 'ויצץ ציץ ויגמול שקדים'. And a proof from Yoma and from the chapter מקום שנהגו, which concludes concerning those things that were hidden away — some say even the staff of Aharon, its almonds and its blossoms were hidden away — implying that there were blossoms and they remained permanently, and on the other side the almonds."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:37.153135788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}